{"Text":"# Enneagram Personality Profiles\n\n## Type 1: The Perfectionist\nType 1s are principled, purposeful, and self-controlled. They strive for improvement and have high standards for themselves and others. They are ethical, responsible, and often feel a strong sense of mission.\n\n## Type 2: The Helper\nType 2s are caring, generous, and people-pleasing. They are driven by a need to be loved and needed. They are empathetic, warm, and supportive but may neglect their own needs while focusing on others.\n\n## Type 3: The Achiever\nType 3s are success-oriented, pragmatic, and adaptive. They excel at setting and achieving goals. They are efficient, image-conscious, and motivated by a fear of failure or worthlessness.\n\n## Type 4: The Individualist\nType 4s are sensitive, introspective, and expressive. They value authenticity and seek meaning in their experiences. They are creative, emotionally honest, and often feel different from others.\n\n## Type 5: The Investigator\nType 5s are perceptive, innovative, and cerebral. They seek knowledge and understanding to feel secure in the world. They are independent, analytical, and often need time alone to recharge.\n\n## Type 6: The Loyalist\nType 6s are committed, security-oriented, and vigilant. They anticipate problems and work to create safety. They are responsible, trustworthy, and value loyalty in relationships.\n\n## Type 7: The Enthusiast\nType 7s are spontaneous, versatile, and optimistic. They seek new experiences and avoid pain or limitation. They are fun-loving, adventurous, and bring positive energy to situations.\n\n## Type 8: The Challenger\nType 8s are powerful, decisive, and self-confident. They protect themselves and those they care about. They are assertive, straightforward, and take charge in challenging situations.\n\n## Type 9: The Peacemaker\nType 9s are receptive, reassuring, and agreeable. They seek harmony and avoid conflict. They are accepting, patient, and good at seeing multiple perspectives.","